* CD4053B triple 2-channel (SPDT) analog multiplexer/demultiplexer
* Behavioral ngspice model, same style as CD4051B.lib
*
* Unofficial model for sample-and-hold / CV switching simulation in KiCad (ngspice).
* It models what matters for S&H work:
*   - A, B, C each select their own switch (A->X, B->Y, C->Z):
*     select low connects X0/Y0/Z0 to the common pin, high connects X1/Y1/Z1
*   - INH high turns all six switches off
*   - logic thresholds at (VDD+VSS)/2
*   - on-resistance (ron), off-resistance (roff)
*   - off-channel leakage (ileak)
*   - charge injection (qinj, total charge per edge at supply span vspan)
*   - channel and common capacitance (cx, ccom)
* It does NOT model: Ron variation with signal level, switching delays,
* break-before-make timing, supply current, ESD clamp diodes to VDD/VEE,
* or crosstalk.
*
* Datasheet Ron (typ/max, at 25 C, shared CD4051B/52B/53B datasheet):
* ~470/1050 ohm @5V, ~180/400 @10V, ~125/240 @15V. The default ron=250 is a
* pessimistic value for a 12 V supply. Charge injection is not specified in
* the datasheet; qinj=5p is an estimate, so check it on the bench if
* accuracy depends on it.
*
* Node order follows the package pin numbers 1..16
* (TI names in brackets: ax/ay = X0/X1, bx/by = Y0/Y1, cx/cy = Z0/Z1):
*   1=Y1 2=Y0 3=Z1 4=Z 5=Z0 6=INH 7=VEE 8=VSS
*   9=C 10=B 11=A 12=X0 13=X1 14=X 15=Y 16=VDD
*
* KiCad Sim.Pins field:
*   1=Y1 2=Y0 3=Z1 4=Z 5=Z0 6=INH 7=VEE 8=VSS 9=C 10=B 11=A 12=X0 13=X1 14=X 15=Y 16=VDD

.subckt CD4053B Y1 Y0 Z1 Z Z0 INH VEE VSS C B A X0 X1 X Y VDD
+ params: ron=250 roff=1e10 ileak=10p qinj=5p cx=5p ccom=9p vspan=12

* ---- Logic inputs: smooth thresholds at half supply (0..1 V logic nodes)
RpA A VSS 1e12
RpB B VSS 1e12
RpC C VSS 1e12
RpINH INH VSS 1e12
BlA lA 0 V = 0.5*(1 + tanh(20*(V(A,VSS) - 0.5*V(VDD,VSS))))
BlB lB 0 V = 0.5*(1 + tanh(20*(V(B,VSS) - 0.5*V(VDD,VSS))))
BlC lC 0 V = 0.5*(1 + tanh(20*(V(C,VSS) - 0.5*V(VDD,VSS))))
BlINH lINH 0 V = 0.5*(1 + tanh(20*(V(INH,VSS) - 0.5*V(VDD,VSS))))

* ---- Switch enables: 0 side when select low, 1 side when high, all off when INH high
BeX0 enX0 0 V = (1-V(lA))*(1-V(lINH))
BeX1 enX1 0 V = (  V(lA))*(1-V(lINH))
BeY0 enY0 0 V = (1-V(lB))*(1-V(lINH))
BeY1 enY1 0 V = (  V(lB))*(1-V(lINH))
BeZ0 enZ0 0 V = (1-V(lC))*(1-V(lINH))
BeZ1 enZ1 0 V = (  V(lC))*(1-V(lINH))

* ---- Internal gate drives swinging VEE..VDD, used for charge injection
BgX0 gX0 0 V = V(VEE) + V(enX0)*V(VDD,VEE)
BgX1 gX1 0 V = V(VEE) + V(enX1)*V(VDD,VEE)
BgY0 gY0 0 V = V(VEE) + V(enY0)*V(VDD,VEE)
BgY1 gY1 0 V = V(VEE) + V(enY1)*V(VDD,VEE)
BgZ0 gZ0 0 V = V(VEE) + V(enZ0)*V(VDD,VEE)
BgZ1 gZ1 0 V = V(VEE) + V(enZ1)*V(VDD,VEE)

* ---- Switches
SX0 X X0 enX0 0 swmod
SX1 X X1 enX1 0 swmod
SY0 Y Y0 enY0 0 swmod
SY1 Y Y1 enY1 0 swmod
SZ0 Z Z0 enZ0 0 swmod
SZ1 Z Z1 enZ1 0 swmod
.model swmod sw vt=0.5 vh=0.1 ron={ron} roff={roff}

* ---- Charge injection: half of qinj into each side of the switch per edge.
* Coupling cap = qinj / (2 * vspan). Set vspan to your VDD-VEE (default 12 V).
.param cinj = {qinj/(2*vspan)}
CiX0a gX0 X0 {cinj}
CiX0b gX0 X {cinj}
CiX1a gX1 X1 {cinj}
CiX1b gX1 X {cinj}
CiY0a gY0 Y0 {cinj}
CiY0b gY0 Y {cinj}
CiY1a gY1 Y1 {cinj}
CiY1b gY1 Y {cinj}
CiZ0a gZ0 Z0 {cinj}
CiZ0b gZ0 Z {cinj}
CiZ1a gZ1 Z1 {cinj}
CiZ1b gZ1 Z {cinj}

* ---- Leakage (toward VEE) and parasitic capacitance
IlX0 X0 VEE {ileak}
IlX1 X1 VEE {ileak}
IlY0 Y0 VEE {ileak}
IlY1 Y1 VEE {ileak}
IlZ0 Z0 VEE {ileak}
IlZ1 Z1 VEE {ileak}
CxX0 X0 VSS {cx}
CxX1 X1 VSS {cx}
CxY0 Y0 VSS {cx}
CxY1 Y1 VSS {cx}
CxZ0 Z0 VSS {cx}
CxZ1 Z1 VSS {cx}
CcX X VSS {ccom}
CcY Y VSS {ccom}
CcZ Z VSS {ccom}

.ends CD4053B
